✅ Cryptographic Evidence Generation
The Reality
Post-quantum migration is not simply replacing RSA or ECC.
It is transforming cryptography from isolated application code into an enterprise-wide governed service.
Organizations that establish cryptographic governance today will be able to adopt tomorrow's algorithms with confidence, speed, and verifiable compliance.
Quantum readiness is not only about stronger cryptography.
It is about governed cryptography.

Quantum is exactly this separation: every governance artifact — decisions, receipts, policy records — is signed with ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) at issuance, not as an afterthought. The signature IS the governance record.
The question raised — "who approved it, when it changed, whether it still complies" — is precisely what an institutionally serious audit chain must answer. Not a dashboard. Not a log. A cryptographically signed, independently verifiable chain where every change has a governed issuer and a verified timestamp.
The organizations that will struggle with PQC migration are not the ones with weak algorithms. They are the ones with no governance layer sitting above the cryptographic layer.
